      "content": "Hey, I'm putting together a preliminary risk brief for a client looking at some emerging market opportunities in West Africa. Can you do a quick stability assessment for a hypothetical country, let's call it 'Zandaria'? \n\nThe demographics are roughly 55% Group A, 25% Group B, 15% Group C, and 5% others. Group A has historically held most of the political offices, while Groups B and C are more concentrated in the resource-rich southern provinces. How much of a risk does this demographic makeup pose for long-term political and social stability?",
